#!/bin/sh
# Mcotis: every commit that changes the app records the change in docs/DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md, the development log shown
# under Help -> Development Plans. Compulsory for every team member and coding agent (AGENTS.md).
# Installed for each clone by the build (src/Mcotis.Desktop/Mcotis.Desktop.csproj sets core.hooksPath to .githooks).
# A change no user can notice (refactor, comment, test-only fix) may say [no-log] in its commit message instead.

msg_file="$1"
grep -qi '\[no-log\]' "$msg_file" && exit 0
# merges carry the entries of the branches they join
[ -f "$(git rev-parse --git-path MERGE_HEAD)" ] && exit 0

changed=$(git diff --cached --name-only)
echo "$changed" | grep -qE '^src/' || exit 0
echo "$changed" | grep -qx 'docs/DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md' && exit 0

cat >&2 <<'MSG'

Commit refused: it changes the app but not docs/DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md.

Add an entry at the top of docs/DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md (Help -> Development Plans shows it to the whole team):

  ## yyyy-mm-dd · What you built
  - Status: Done | In progress | Planned
  - Who: your name
  - Where: menu path / window / tab (or the code area)
  - What: what it does, in a sentence or two
  - Checks: the --flag of the checks that prove it, or "none yet"

then stage it (git add docs/DEVELOPMENT_LOG.md) and commit again.
Only for a change no user can notice, write [no-log] in the commit message.

MSG
exit 1
